## Executive Summary

MiMo V2.6 Pro is Xiaomi's flagship open-weight mixture-of-experts model from their MiMo series, released September 22, 2026, designed for complex, long-horizon agentic workflows. It features a massive 1.02 trillion total parameters (42 billion active per token), 1M token context window, native multimodal capabilities (text, image, audio, video), and exceptional performance on coding and agentic benchmarks (89.9% on Terminal-Bench 2.1, 71.9% on DeepSWE v1.1, 63.2% on MiMo Code Bench, 76.9% on Toolathlon-Verified, 82.0% on OSWorld-Verified, 53.1 on AutomationBench v1.0.6). The model ranks #1 of 114 on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index (46), ranking #13 of 229 on BenchLM with 73.6/100. MiMo V2.6 Pro is the first open-weight model to reach the 1-trillion-parameter class, with full weights available on Hugging Face under an MIT license. The model is priced at $0.435/$0.87 per 1M tokens (OpenRouter: $0.3698/$0.7395 with 15% discount), making it a competitive option for organizations seeking open-weight frontier models with strong performance on coding and agentic tasks.

---

## Model Identity and Background

**Developer:** Xiaomi
**Release Date:** September 22, 2026
**Series:** MiMo V2.6 (MiMo V2.6 Pro, MiMo V2.6 Flash)
**Predecessor:** MiMo V2.5 Pro (June 2026, retired October 21, 2026)
**Successor:** No successor yet
**License:** MIT license (open weights available on Hugging Face)
**Context Window:** 1,050,000 tokens
**Max Output:** 64,000 tokens

MiMo V2.6 Pro is Xiaomi's flagship open-weight mixture-of-experts model from their MiMo series, released September 22, 2026. The model is designed for complex, long-horizon agentic workflows, featuring a massive 1.02 trillion total parameters (42 billion active per token) and a 1M token context window. MiMo V2.6 Pro uses Grouped Query Attention (GQA) with Sliding Window Attention (SWA) at a tiny 128-token window size, demonstrating that simple architecture design can achieve state-of-the-art performance. The model was released alongside MiMo V2.6 Flash (309B parameters, $0.14/$0.28 per 1M tokens), which is designed for cost-sensitive applications. MiMo V2.6 Pro represents a significant advancement over MiMo V2.5 Pro, with substantial improvements on agentic and coding benchmarks.

